title: Veeam: Backup proxy
agents: special
catalog: os/storage
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors a backup proxy of a Veeam Backup & Replication server,
 collected via the Veeam special agent. It reports the proxy type,
 description, host and its online, disabled and out-of-date states.

 This check is {CRIT} if the proxy is offline, since an unreachable proxy
 cannot run a backup. It is {WARN} if the proxy's components are out of
 date. It is {WARN} by default if the proxy is disabled; the state is
 configurable, since a deliberately disabled proxy is normal in some
 estates. These three states are evaluated independently: a proxy can be
 online and disabled, or offline and enabled, at the same time.

discovery:
 One service is created for each backup proxy reported by the API.

item:
 The name of the backup proxy.
